[h1]Marry a Local Noble - Continued[/h1]

Adds character interactions to marry your dynasty's characters to a local noble. Three tiers available depending on how much you want to invest in the match.

This is an updated and fixed version of [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3600093580]Kaiser's original mod[/url], rewritten from scratch for compatibility with [b]version 1.2[/b].

[h2]Marriage Tiers[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Prominent Noble (25 ducats)[/b] - a noble of good standing with strong abilities (30-75 stats)
[*][b]Local Noble (10 ducats)[/b] - a noble of modest standing with average abilities (20-50 stats)
[*][b]Minor Noble (free)[/b] - a noble of little distinction with low abilities (10-30 stats)
[/list]

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*]Works for both [b]male and female[/b] recipients
[*]Created noble shares the recipient's [b]culture and religion[/b]
[*]AI will use the 25 ducat interaction to keep old rulers from going unmarried
[*]Compatible with [b]any government type[/b] (monarchy, republic, tribe, steppe horde; theocracy support gated by church marriage laws)
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
Should be compatible with any mod. Adds character interactions and a localization file with no base game files overridden.

Works alongside [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3681629733]Nobles Auto Marry - Continued[/url]. If that mod marries off your intended recipient before this interaction fires, the ducats are automatically refunded.

Requires EU5 patch [b]1.2.x[/b].

[h2]Source[/h2]
[url=https://github.com/JustinRudisal/marry-local-noble]GitHub[/url]

[h2]Credits[/h2]
All credit for the concept goes to [b]Kaiser[/b]. This version adds compatibility updates, bug fixes, and the tiered pricing system.
